  "body_html": "<h1>Simple Game</h1>\n<p>A <strong>simple game</strong> is a coalitional game whose coalitions are classified as\nlosing or winning. In characteristic-function form,\n$$\n  v(S) \\in \\{0,1\\}\n$$\nfor every coalition $S \\subseteq N$, and the grand coalition is winning:\n$$\n  v(N)=1.\n$$</p>\n<p>A coalition $S$ is <strong>winning</strong> when $v(S)=1$.</p>\n<p>Simple games model yes/no collective decision rules. Later refinements such\nas weighted majority games add an explicit quota-and-weight representation.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[MSZ Ch.16, Def 16.2] Maschler, Solan, Zamir, <em>Game Theory</em>.</li>\n</ul>",
